# Commit messages

All staging and commits are manual repository-owner actions. Agents must never run `git add`, `git commit`, or otherwise stage or commit files, even when explicitly asked.

When the user asks for a commit message (e.g. "provide the commit message", "commit message"):

- **Only** reply with the message in chat (optionally in a fenced code block for easy copy)

## Format

Conventional Commits, **one short line**:

```
<type>: <concise summary>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `style`, `test`, `ci`

Optional scope: `feat(db): add initial migration`

## Rules

- Imperative mood, lowercase summary after the type (no period at the end)
- Focus on **why/what changed**, not a file list
- Keep it short — no paragraphs, no bullet body unless they ask
- Match the staged/working tree changes when suggesting

## Examples

```
feat: wire EF SQLite DI and initial migration
fix: qualify Maui Application base type
refactor: drop soft delete from Base
chore: target Windows-only TFM
ci: add GitHub Actions Windows build
```
